WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:38.010
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:38.280 --> 01:43.900
[Small Town Remedy]

3
01:44.140 --> 01:46.750
[Episode 9]

4
01:57.570 --> 01:59.289
[Operating Room Anteroom]

5
02:01.560 --> 02:02.640
Sterile gauze.

6
02:03.000 --> 02:03.640
Coming.

7
02:07.310 --> 02:07.790
Here.

8
02:09.080 --> 02:11.150
The patient was struck on the left side.

9
02:11.150 --> 02:12.150
When she fell,

10
02:12.240 --> 02:13.800
the right side of her head hit the ground.

11
02:13.800 --> 02:15.960
The patient has a depressed fracture of the left temporal region,

12
02:15.960 --> 02:17.750
a left-sided cerebral contusion and laceration,

13
02:17.750 --> 02:20.210
and a small right-sided subdural hematoma.

14
02:20.960 --> 02:23.400
There's a marked midline shift to the right.

15
02:23.400 --> 02:24.240
The patient's left pupil

16
02:24.240 --> 02:25.970
is now significantly dilated.

17
02:26.120 --> 02:28.380
We need to remove the hematoma on the left

18
02:28.590 --> 02:30.000
and perform a decompressive craniectomy.

19
02:30.000 --> 02:30.750
If there are significant changes

20
02:30.750 --> 02:31.840
on the right side,

21
02:31.870 --> 02:32.590
we'll deal with them then.

22
02:32.590 --> 02:34.520
The fracture is at least 10 cm long.

23
02:34.710 --> 02:35.840
How did that happen?

24
02:37.360 --> 02:39.090
Her husband hit her with a club.

25
02:41.710 --> 02:42.520
What the hell?

26
02:43.030 --> 02:44.000
Is he even human?

27
02:44.000 --> 02:44.710
Did anyone call the police?

28
02:44.710 --> 02:45.840
Calm down first.

29
02:46.360 --> 02:47.560
The patient's family said

30
02:47.560 --> 02:49.220
the police had taken him away.

31
02:49.280 --> 02:49.990
Keep your emotions

32
02:49.990 --> 02:50.920
out of your work.

33
02:51.710 --> 02:53.840
And what if, after we finish...

34
02:55.030 --> 02:56.630
the pressure on the left side drops,

35
02:56.630 --> 02:57.800
but the bleeding on the right side increases?

36
02:57.800 --> 02:58.560
What do we do then?

37
02:58.560 --> 02:59.620
Povidone-iodine.

38
03:00.680 --> 03:03.150
If there's significant bleeding on the right side,

39
03:03.150 --> 03:05.550
we'll have to perform another craniotomy.

40
03:05.750 --> 03:07.080
We'll see whether we can

41
03:07.910 --> 03:09.000
preserve her bone flaps.

42
03:09.000 --> 03:09.960
If we can't,

43
03:10.280 --> 03:12.810
she'll have a big dent on each side of her head.

44
03:12.840 --> 03:14.360
How is she supposed to live like that?

45
03:14.360 --> 03:15.680
This is no time for that.

46
03:15.680 --> 03:16.810
Save her life first.

47
03:17.430 --> 03:19.760
Nothing matters more than staying alive.

48
03:21.490 --> 03:23.300
[Operating Room Integrated Control System]

49
03:33.960 --> 03:35.310
The depressed skull fracture

50
03:35.310 --> 03:37.079
caused by the assault

51
03:37.310 --> 03:39.120
has resulted in some adhesion

52
03:39.120 --> 03:41.079
between the inner surface of the skull and the dura mater.

53
03:41.079 --> 03:42.360
Separating the bone flap

54
03:42.360 --> 03:43.310
carries a high risk of causing

55
03:43.310 --> 03:45.800
further damage to the brain tissue beneath the dura.

56
03:45.800 --> 03:47.150
I'll use rongeurs to remove

57
03:47.150 --> 03:48.680
the skull fragments first.

58
04:01.190 --> 04:02.310
Neuro dissector.

59
04:07.840 --> 04:08.970
The bone flap is off.

60
04:09.030 --> 04:10.690
Now opening the dura further.

61
04:11.600 --> 04:14.020
[Operating Room Integrated Control System]

62
04:24.270 --> 04:26.270
Once we've finished removing the hematoma,

63
04:26.270 --> 04:27.510
we also need to place

64
04:27.510 --> 04:29.510
an intracranial pressure monitor in the ventricle.

65
04:29.510 --> 04:31.310
Have you performed a ventricular puncture before?

66
04:31.310 --> 04:32.070
Yes.

67
04:32.150 --> 04:33.270
You'll do it later.

68
04:36.159 --> 04:36.750
But I've never done it

69
04:36.750 --> 04:39.040
on a patient with such severe brain injuries before.

70
04:39.040 --> 04:39.770
Give it a try.

71
04:41.240 --> 04:43.159
W-Why aren't you doing it yourself?

72
04:43.159 --> 04:44.760
If you can't, I'll take over.

73
05:06.040 --> 05:07.720
I followed the trajectory for ventricular puncture...

74
05:07.720 --> 05:09.180
the puncture trajectory.

75
05:09.430 --> 05:10.720
Why isn't any cerebrospinal fluid coming out?

76
05:10.720 --> 05:11.980
Think carefully about

77
05:12.240 --> 05:14.970
the patient's current intracranial condition.

78
05:15.560 --> 05:17.560
There's significant displacement of the brain tissue.

79
05:17.560 --> 05:18.720
Shouldn't the direction

80
05:18.720 --> 05:20.980
of your needle be adjusted accordingly?

81
05:51.800 --> 05:53.000
The CSF is coming out.

82
05:53.070 --> 05:53.800
That's good.

83
05:58.830 --> 06:02.650
[Beijing Time] [Elapsed Time]

84
06:08.680 --> 06:10.810
The left pupil has returned to normal.

85
06:12.040 --> 06:13.370
The right one is normal.

86
06:15.040 --> 06:16.480
The intracranial pressure is still a bit high.

87
06:16.480 --> 06:17.310
To be safe,

88
06:17.510 --> 06:18.510
give her a CT scan.

89
06:18.690 --> 06:22.140
[Emergency; 18]

90
06:20.430 --> 06:21.070
You do it.

91
06:22.390 --> 06:23.190
I can't.

92
06:23.950 --> 06:25.160
I haven't been in an operating room in 2 years.

93
06:25.160 --> 06:26.360
Call Che Mingming.

94
06:27.040 --> 06:28.970
Tell her to come over immediately.

95
06:31.430 --> 06:32.110
Junnan.

96
06:33.310 --> 06:33.830
Junnan!

97
06:36.390 --> 06:37.320
Why are you here?

98
06:37.870 --> 06:39.930
I need to talk to you about something.

99
06:41.560 --> 06:43.510
The bleeding on the right has increased significantly.

100
06:43.510 --> 06:44.710
What about the pupil?

101
06:46.680 --> 06:47.880
The pupil is dilated.

102
06:49.430 --> 06:51.000
Then we'll have to remove the hematoma on the other side

103
06:51.000 --> 06:53.270
and perform a decompressive craniectomy there too.

104
06:53.270 --> 06:54.120
Now she really will have

105
06:54.120 --> 06:55.780
a dent on each side of her head.

106
06:56.040 --> 06:57.070
But you're right.

107
06:57.120 --> 06:58.870
Staying alive matters more than anything.

108
06:58.870 --> 07:00.070
There's no other way.

109
07:00.070 --> 07:01.510
She'll have to wait until she recovers

110
07:01.510 --> 07:02.830
and then have reconstructive surgery.

111
07:02.830 --> 07:04.760
Prepare to evacuate the hematoma.

112
07:07.560 --> 07:08.560
Is the angle okay?

113
07:08.750 --> 07:09.310
Yes.

114
07:09.870 --> 07:11.670
Now irrigate the surgical site.

115
07:18.120 --> 07:19.630
We need to remove the hematoma

116
07:19.630 --> 07:20.720
and the nonviable brain tissue

117
07:20.720 --> 07:22.120
from the lacerated brain

118
07:22.870 --> 07:25.360
while protecting the surrounding brain tissue

119
07:25.360 --> 07:27.750
that remains relatively intact and functional.

120
07:27.750 --> 07:29.360
This requires a higher level of precision

121
07:29.360 --> 07:30.360
in the operation.

122
07:32.190 --> 07:33.050
Adjust it a bit.

123
07:48.430 --> 07:49.920
You're good at the sing-and-dance duet.

124
07:49.920 --> 07:50.780
Who taught you?

125
07:51.830 --> 07:52.760
I taught myself.

126
07:55.720 --> 07:57.180
You did a good job just now.

127
07:57.800 --> 07:59.510
Um, I think you...

128
08:00.360 --> 08:01.760
have at least a 50% chance

129
08:01.830 --> 08:03.630
of getting into the PhD program.

130
08:04.560 --> 08:05.720
Only 50%?

131
08:06.430 --> 08:07.070
Doctors never

132
08:07.070 --> 08:08.390
speak in absolutes.

133
08:09.360 --> 08:11.890
Besides, a 50% chance is already pretty good.

134
08:13.160 --> 08:14.510
You're really something.

135
08:14.510 --> 08:15.290
Even your compliments

136
08:15.290 --> 08:16.550
come out sounding off.

137
08:18.950 --> 08:19.430
But...

138
08:20.240 --> 08:20.830
Um,

139
08:20.830 --> 08:22.690
you still have other advantages.

140
08:22.920 --> 08:24.950
For example, um...

141
08:22.950 --> 08:25.990
[No smoking]

142
08:26.390 --> 08:27.160
Enough, enough.

143
08:27.160 --> 08:28.430
Stop stumbling over your words.

144
08:28.430 --> 08:30.270
I know you're not good at saying thanks

145
08:30.270 --> 08:31.270
or apologizing.

146
08:32.000 --> 08:33.860
Message received on both counts.

147
08:35.320 --> 08:36.630
If you have any questions about the PhD exams,

148
08:36.630 --> 08:38.159
feel free to ask me anytime.

149
08:39.390 --> 08:40.990
Then thank you, Zhengliang!

150
08:41.750 --> 08:42.669
My heart

151
08:42.409 --> 08:45.200
[Quiet]

152
08:43.510 --> 08:44.840
is pounding like crazy.

153
08:45.390 --> 08:47.270
Thump, thump, thump.

154
08:49.240 --> 08:50.440
My mom had

155
08:51.000 --> 08:52.730
heart problems back in the day.

156
08:53.030 --> 08:54.270
Do you think I might have...

157
08:54.270 --> 08:55.750
Don't overthink it. Don't overthink it.

158
08:55.750 --> 08:57.320
Let me see if I can... try a trick on you.

159
08:57.320 --> 08:58.840
Why are you w-worrying so much?

160
08:58.840 --> 08:59.320
Let me see

161
08:59.320 --> 09:00.080
if I can ease it for you.

162
09:00.080 --> 09:01.550
Do I need to take any medication?

163
09:01.550 --> 09:02.480
No need, no need.

164
09:02.720 --> 09:03.360
My heart is thumping...

165
09:03.360 --> 09:03.820
Come on.

166
09:06.030 --> 09:07.560
Let's try this. Just relax.

167
09:08.030 --> 09:10.320
You need to calm yourself down first.

168
09:10.320 --> 09:12.000
Come on. Come on.

169
09:12.360 --> 09:13.390
Come on, this might feel a little cold.

170
09:13.390 --> 09:14.910
Bear with it. Bear with it.

171
09:14.960 --> 09:15.890
Come on. Come on.

172
09:16.150 --> 09:18.000
Come on, breathe out. Breathe out.

173
09:18.000 --> 09:19.460
That's it. Now breathe in.

174
09:20.000 --> 09:21.550
Breathe in. Hold it, hold it.

175
09:21.550 --> 09:23.360
Come on, now breathe out.

176
09:26.080 --> 09:27.630
There's n-nothing else wrong with you.

177
09:27.630 --> 09:28.490
Nothing at all.

178
09:28.670 --> 09:30.630
Try to manage your emotions.

179
09:32.000 --> 09:33.550
Come out. I need to talk to you.

180
09:33.550 --> 09:34.480
Perfect timing.

181
09:35.120 --> 09:36.780
Zhengguang was here earlier.

182
09:37.030 --> 09:38.760
He asked me to pass on a message.

183
09:38.790 --> 09:40.360
He wants you to move back home.

184
09:40.360 --> 09:41.620
He's going to Beijing.

185
09:44.030 --> 09:44.830
What's wrong?

186
09:45.750 --> 09:47.680
Why did you want to become a doctor?

187
09:49.240 --> 09:50.510
I never wanted to be a doctor.

188
09:50.510 --> 09:52.630
My dad wanted me to be one.

189
09:52.630 --> 09:53.080
Fine.

190
09:53.600 --> 09:54.670
Then what do you want to do?

191
09:54.670 --> 09:55.150
I...

192
09:57.120 --> 09:58.750
I don't know what I want to do.

193
09:58.910 --> 10:00.710
But I know what I don't want to do.

194
10:01.750 --> 10:03.750
I don't want to... perform surgery.

195
10:05.270 --> 10:07.480
Because whenever I step into

196
10:07.480 --> 10:09.080
the operating room, I panic.

197
10:09.150 --> 10:10.790
Well, if I do surgery on a patient

198
10:10.790 --> 10:11.510
and mess it up,

199
10:11.510 --> 10:13.320
isn't that the same as harming them?

200
10:13.320 --> 10:14.080
So you're worried

201
10:14.080 --> 10:15.240
your skills aren't good enough,

202
10:15.240 --> 10:16.440
and you're afraid to operate.

203
10:16.440 --> 10:17.120
On the surface,

204
10:17.120 --> 10:18.200
it looks like you're thinking about what's best for the patients

205
10:18.200 --> 10:19.360
and taking responsibility for them,

206
10:19.360 --> 10:20.960
but in reality you're just avoiding the problem.

207
10:20.960 --> 10:22.270
No, I'm not avoiding anything.

208
10:22.270 --> 10:23.510
Not every doctor

209
10:23.510 --> 10:25.000
has to perform surgery, right?

210
10:25.000 --> 10:26.360
Some doctors, like you,

211
10:26.550 --> 10:28.270
are suited to operating.

212
10:28.360 --> 10:29.510
And someone like me

213
10:29.550 --> 10:30.600
is suited to providing

214
10:30.600 --> 10:32.400
emotional support to patients.

215
10:33.120 --> 10:35.720
I just want to work shifts and prescribe medication.

216
10:35.720 --> 10:37.380
That's a way of living, right?

217
10:48.120 --> 10:49.320
Do you think...

218
10:51.390 --> 10:52.670
I don't deserve to be a doctor?

219
10:52.670 --> 10:53.670
Yes, I do think so.

220
11:21.550 --> 11:23.210
The surgery went as expected.

221
11:23.750 --> 11:25.510
We'll monitor her for a few days.

222
11:25.510 --> 11:26.150
She may

223
11:26.150 --> 11:28.210
need reconstructive surgery later.

224
11:29.910 --> 11:31.510
How much more will that cost?

225
11:31.600 --> 11:33.360
Your deposit is enough for now.

226
11:34.150 --> 11:35.950
Once her condition stabilizes,

227
11:36.440 --> 11:38.300
repairing both sides of her skull

228
11:39.790 --> 11:41.990
will cost around 70,000 to 80,000 yuan.

229
11:43.000 --> 11:45.360
We retired a couple of years ago.

230
11:45.870 --> 11:46.720
At our age,

231
11:46.720 --> 11:48.390
we're still working at a hotel.

232
11:48.390 --> 11:51.050
We can't come up with that much money all at once.

233
11:54.150 --> 11:55.510
But if you don't do it,

234
11:55.960 --> 11:57.030
she'll have dents

235
11:57.240 --> 11:59.360
on both sides of her head from now on.

236
12:00.600 --> 12:02.800
It would really affect her appearance.

237
12:13.520 --> 12:18.390
[Family Members Not Allowed]

238
12:39.050 --> 12:41.040
[Family Members Not Allowed]

239
12:53.120 --> 12:54.450
Is Liu Zhengguang here?

240
12:55.080 --> 12:56.200
He left a long time ago.

241
12:56.200 --> 12:57.860
Do you need him for something?

242
12:58.480 --> 13:00.240
He came to the hospital this afternoon

243
13:00.240 --> 13:01.790
and asked Chen Junnan to tell me something.

244
13:01.790 --> 13:03.450
He said he's going to Beijing.

245
13:04.080 --> 13:06.140
Do you know why he's going to Beijing?

246
13:06.270 --> 13:07.800
Why don't you just call him?

247
13:09.600 --> 13:10.800
Let me think about it.

248
13:10.960 --> 13:12.560
What's there to think about?

249
13:13.000 --> 13:14.600
You obviously care about him.

250
13:14.600 --> 13:16.150
You're brothers. What's so hard about expressing your feelings?

251
13:16.150 --> 13:17.600
It's not that I care about him.

252
13:17.600 --> 13:17.960
I...

253
13:18.840 --> 13:19.670
I'm just afraid he'll...

254
13:19.670 --> 13:20.720
he'll cause more trouble.

255
13:20.720 --> 13:21.510
Fine, fine.

256
13:22.910 --> 13:23.630
I give up.

257
13:23.630 --> 13:24.870
You two are exactly alike—

258
13:24.870 --> 13:26.200
both stubborn as mules.

259
13:27.840 --> 13:29.770
You're getting off work this late?

260
13:29.790 --> 13:30.840
You're going back alone.

261
13:30.840 --> 13:31.900
Aren't you scared?

262
13:36.600 --> 13:38.000
Are you worried about me?

263
13:39.840 --> 13:41.570
Then do you want to walk me home?

264
13:43.750 --> 13:45.350
We're not that close, are we?

265
13:45.720 --> 13:46.790
I've still got a shift to finish.

266
13:46.790 --> 13:47.790
Go back to work!

267
13:48.440 --> 13:49.720
Why even say it?

268
13:51.840 --> 13:52.700
D-Don't worry.

269
13:52.960 --> 13:54.760
I'm not going home alone anyway.

270
13:56.640 --> 13:58.600
[1314 Funeral Services]

271
13:57.390 --> 13:59.360
I've been watching you for a while.

272
14:00.360 --> 14:01.820
You've got your eye on him,

273
14:02.320 --> 14:03.790
and I've got my eye on you.

274
14:12.550 --> 14:14.480
So, Liu Zhengliang...

275
14:14.630 --> 14:16.090
You're serious about him?

276
14:16.390 --> 14:17.200
Yeah.

277
14:18.670 --> 14:20.120
Then how does he feel about you?

278
14:20.120 --> 14:21.550
Who cares?

279
14:22.200 --> 14:24.460
I'll win him over sooner or later anyway.

280
14:25.720 --> 14:26.440
Back then,

281
14:26.440 --> 14:28.120
was it also Mom who pursued you first?

282
14:28.120 --> 14:29.270
Not exactly.

283
14:30.390 --> 14:33.320
There were plenty of guys chasing your mom back then.

284
14:33.320 --> 14:34.720
Some were richer than me.

285
14:35.120 --> 14:36.520
Some were more handsome.

286
14:36.720 --> 14:38.750
Then why did I have the last laugh?

287
14:39.510 --> 14:40.390
That's because

288
14:40.670 --> 14:42.080
I dared to risk my life

289
14:42.510 --> 14:44.320
for your mom.

290
14:47.910 --> 14:48.870
That bunch...

291
14:49.030 --> 14:51.160
That bunch of young punks chasing her?

292
14:51.360 --> 14:52.630
I'd beat up every one that showed up.

293
14:52.630 --> 14:53.720
Every single one.

294
14:56.510 --> 14:58.030
What year do you think this is?

295
14:58.030 --> 14:59.480
Who still fights like that?

296
14:59.480 --> 14:59.840
Well,

297
14:59.840 --> 15:00.910
I mean,

298
15:01.550 --> 15:03.390
your mom was indeed pretty back then,

299
15:03.390 --> 15:05.120
but not as pretty as you.

300
15:05.910 --> 15:07.750
A daughter as great as mine

301
15:08.790 --> 15:11.870
deserves a man

302
15:12.150 --> 15:14.120
who'd risk everything for her.

303
15:15.910 --> 15:16.720
Dad.

304
15:17.600 --> 15:18.660
I'm your daughter.

305
15:21.910 --> 15:23.240
If you can give everything

306
15:23.240 --> 15:24.570
for the person you love,

307
15:25.840 --> 15:26.630
then so can I.

308
15:33.840 --> 15:34.630
Coming.

309
15:38.910 --> 15:39.840
What's the deal?

310
15:40.270 --> 15:41.670
You're going to Beijing?

311
15:41.910 --> 15:42.910
Who told you that?

312
15:43.120 --> 15:43.910
Didn't you ask Chen Junnan

313
15:43.910 --> 15:44.870
to tell me?

314
15:46.240 --> 15:47.910
I asked him to tell you to move back home,

315
15:47.910 --> 15:49.970
not to tell you I was going to Beijing.

316
15:52.600 --> 15:54.530
I don't want to move back right now.

317
15:55.270 --> 15:56.270
Suit yourself.

318
15:57.150 --> 15:58.750
I just don't want the apartment sitting empty and going to waste.

319
15:58.750 --> 15:59.670
If you don't want to live here,

320
15:59.670 --> 16:00.910
you can live wherever you want.

321
16:00.910 --> 16:02.370
Don't change the subject.

322
16:03.200 --> 16:04.800
Why are you going to Beijing?

323
16:07.840 --> 16:08.600
Because I've lived

324
16:08.600 --> 16:10.000
in Fucheng my whole life.

325
16:10.440 --> 16:12.100
I want to go out and try my luck!

326
16:12.550 --> 16:14.210
What's that got to do with you?

327
16:14.360 --> 16:15.150
Mind your own business.

328
16:15.150 --> 16:16.880
Who said I was going to stop you?

329
16:17.320 --> 16:18.150
Just do me a favor and let me know

330
16:18.150 --> 16:19.150
when you leave.

331
16:19.910 --> 16:21.720
I'll move back in after you leave.

332
16:21.720 --> 16:22.580
I'm off to work.

333
16:23.960 --> 16:24.890
Liu Zhengliang!

334
16:29.550 --> 16:31.480
Aren't you afraid I won't find a job

335
16:31.550 --> 16:32.960
and will starve to death out there?

336
16:32.960 --> 16:33.840
What if I end up

337
16:34.320 --> 16:35.670
sleeping on the streets and turning to crime?

338
16:35.670 --> 16:37.000
What if I commit a crime?

339
16:39.270 --> 16:40.120
What are you laughing at?

340
16:40.120 --> 16:41.050
Liu Zhengguang,

341
16:41.240 --> 16:42.720
stop making me laugh.

342
16:43.750 --> 16:44.720
"Startup Dreams: Beijing, Shanghai & Guangzhou"—

343
16:44.370 --> 16:46.510
[Startup Dreams: Beijing, Shanghai & Guangzhou]

344
16:44.720 --> 16:46.120
can you even follow this?

345
16:46.630 --> 16:47.840
And turning to crime?

346
16:48.150 --> 16:49.550
Do you even have the guts?

347
16:50.670 --> 16:51.750
Who do you think you're looking down on?

348
16:51.750 --> 16:53.120
Come back if you can't make it.

349
16:53.120 --> 16:53.790
Call me if you can't

350
16:53.790 --> 16:54.600
afford a ticket.

351
16:54.600 --> 16:55.870
Otherwise, don't contact me.

352
16:55.870 --> 16:56.840
Listen here, Liu Zhengliang.

353
16:56.840 --> 16:57.790
I definitely won't call you.

354
16:57.790 --> 16:59.270
I definitely won't contact you.

355
16:59.270 --> 17:00.150
I'm telling you,

356
17:00.150 --> 17:01.030
I have plenty of people I can turn to.

357
17:01.030 --> 17:02.030
I can call Ai Chen,

358
17:02.120 --> 17:03.670
Jia Xin, Cai Zhuzi,

359
17:03.670 --> 17:05.400
Chen Junnan, Che Mingming,

360
17:05.510 --> 17:07.240
my Uncle Dong, or even old Wu next door!

361
17:07.240 --> 17:09.700
I'd call any of them before I'd ever call you!

362
17:17.349 --> 17:18.160
Mingming.

363
17:19.680 --> 17:21.480
Thanks. Thanks for the coffee.

364
17:22.069 --> 17:23.069
Don't mention it.

365
17:25.030 --> 17:26.359
Are you feeling better?

366
17:26.589 --> 17:28.050
I'm not upset or anything.

367
17:33.440 --> 17:34.720
Liu Zhengliang can be

368
17:35.030 --> 17:37.110
pretty harsh with his words sometimes,

369
17:37.110 --> 17:38.910
and what he says can really hurt.

370
17:39.880 --> 17:40.680
But...

371
17:41.790 --> 17:43.720
it's not because he's wrong.

372
17:44.440 --> 17:45.400
It's precisely

373
17:45.400 --> 17:47.400
because he's usually right.

374
17:51.000 --> 17:51.790
I know.

375
17:53.000 --> 17:55.260
But how does it affect him if I just coast?

376
17:59.070 --> 17:59.960
Exactly.

377
18:00.000 --> 18:01.590
It's because you can't affect him

378
18:01.590 --> 18:03.850
that he's genuinely looking out for you.

379
18:03.960 --> 18:05.110
What he means is,

380
18:05.440 --> 18:06.310
either

381
18:06.310 --> 18:08.310
you work hard to improve your skills

382
18:08.480 --> 18:10.270
or you change careers ASAP.

383
18:10.590 --> 18:11.830
Just find something you enjoy

384
18:11.830 --> 18:12.960
and are good at.

385
18:12.960 --> 18:14.070
Wouldn't that be better?

386
18:14.070 --> 18:15.000
Don't you think?

387
18:20.310 --> 18:22.030
You could put it that way.

388
18:27.720 --> 18:29.030
I actually think

389
18:29.480 --> 18:30.160
he is more of

390
18:30.160 --> 18:31.590
a Northeasterner than many people

391
18:31.590 --> 18:32.520
who grew up here.

392
18:33.400 --> 18:34.790
Unlike some people who seem

393
18:34.790 --> 18:36.640
generous and genuine on the surface

394
18:36.640 --> 18:37.880
but are all

395
18:38.110 --> 18:39.440
just putting on a show.

396
18:42.640 --> 18:44.840
You're quite a good judge of character.

397
18:47.310 --> 18:48.840
Which newly divorced woman

398
18:48.880 --> 18:50.410
wouldn't be clear-headed?

399
19:04.310 --> 19:05.040
What is this?

400
19:10.720 --> 19:12.110
Sweet potatoes?

401
19:12.480 --> 19:12.960
What?

402
19:12.960 --> 19:14.720
Trying to apologize to me with sweet potatoes?

403
19:14.720 --> 19:15.790
What are you talking about?

404
19:15.790 --> 19:17.390
Why would I apologize to you?

405
19:18.030 --> 19:19.160
Are there any for me?

406
19:19.880 --> 19:20.440
I don't want any.

407
19:20.440 --> 19:22.040
I bought two. You guys share.

408
19:22.110 --> 19:23.770
I checked him over. He's fine.

409
19:24.480 --> 19:25.200
Mingming.

410
19:26.350 --> 19:27.880
-What are you three eating? -Thank you, Zhengliang.

411
19:27.880 --> 19:28.920
Leaving me out, huh?

412
19:28.920 --> 19:30.250
I didn't buy any for you.

413
19:32.470 --> 19:33.240
So blunt.

414
19:33.240 --> 19:34.440
I don't want any. I...

415
19:34.880 --> 19:36.680
I get heartburn if I eat too much.

416
19:39.750 --> 19:40.310
Come on.

417
19:40.750 --> 19:42.280
Help me finish some of this.

418
19:43.070 --> 19:45.200
Mingming gave it to me. I have to eat it.

419
19:48.070 --> 19:48.680
Come on.

420
19:49.350 --> 19:50.480
Help me eat some.

421
19:50.720 --> 19:51.980
I said I don't want any.

422
19:52.070 --> 19:53.070
Come on.

423
19:53.270 --> 19:54.200
Just try a piece.

424
20:06.440 --> 20:07.100
Is it sweet?

425
20:07.480 --> 20:08.160
Sweet or not?

426
20:08.160 --> 20:08.880
Is it sweet?

427
20:10.550 --> 20:12.080
Say something. Is it sweet?

428
20:14.680 --> 20:16.200
Really sweet. Super sweet.

429
20:16.200 --> 20:17.000
Super sweet.

430
20:17.270 --> 20:19.600
It must be from the old man at the entrance.

431
20:22.640 --> 20:24.350
-I can tell by the taste it's from him. -Doctor!

432
20:24.350 --> 20:25.110
Doctor!

433
20:29.510 --> 20:32.110
Jiao... Jiao woke up.

434
20:45.160 --> 20:45.880
Jiao?

435
20:47.000 --> 20:47.680
Jiao?

436
20:48.750 --> 20:49.550
The penlight.

437
21:00.550 --> 21:01.720
Has Jiao shown any signs

438
21:01.720 --> 21:03.320
of voluntary limb movement?

439
21:03.830 --> 21:04.960
-No. -No.

440
21:07.640 --> 21:08.840
Then it seems Jiao...

441
21:08.960 --> 21:10.820
hasn't regained consciousness.

442
21:11.510 --> 21:12.400
No way.

443
21:12.830 --> 21:13.510
I-I saw her

444
21:13.510 --> 21:14.640
open her eyes.

445
21:15.830 --> 21:16.550
Zhang.

446
21:16.830 --> 21:18.290
You saw it too, didn't you?

447
21:18.590 --> 21:19.510
Tell the doctors.

448
21:19.510 --> 21:20.000
Yes.

449
21:20.000 --> 21:22.680
Tell them I wasn't making it up! -Yes, I saw it too.

450
21:22.680 --> 21:23.810
She opened her eyes!

451
21:26.440 --> 21:28.790
That was an involuntary neurological reflex.

452
21:28.790 --> 21:30.200
It's fairly common.

453
21:31.000 --> 21:31.680
It can't be taken as

454
21:31.680 --> 21:33.680
proof that the patient has woken up.

455
21:48.590 --> 21:49.550
Dr. Liu,

456
21:50.310 --> 21:51.880
is it a good sign

457
21:52.400 --> 21:53.860
that Jiao opened her eyes?

458
21:54.000 --> 21:56.000
She's never opened her eyes before.

459
21:59.920 --> 22:01.650
Sometimes, hopes do come true.

460
22:02.750 --> 22:03.720
So I...

461
22:04.750 --> 22:06.680
told my first lie

462
22:06.880 --> 22:07.920
as a doctor.

463
22:08.240 --> 22:08.720
Yes.

464
22:09.960 --> 22:10.890
It's a good sign.

465
22:12.680 --> 22:13.920
It means Jiao's

466
22:13.920 --> 22:15.640
chances of regaining consciousness

467
22:15.640 --> 22:16.500
have improved.

468
22:18.160 --> 22:19.640
Are you telling the truth?

469
22:21.880 --> 22:23.070
Yes. Yes.

470
22:24.160 --> 22:24.920
So,

471
22:24.920 --> 22:26.270
whenever you have time,

472
22:26.270 --> 22:27.270
try talking to her more.

473
22:27.270 --> 22:28.160
It will help.

474
22:28.480 --> 22:29.110
If anything similar

475
22:29.110 --> 22:30.310
happens again,

476
22:30.680 --> 22:31.790
call us anytime.

477
22:31.790 --> 22:33.270
Okay, okay.

478
22:33.550 --> 22:35.110
Okay, okay.

479
22:35.110 --> 22:36.720
Thank you. Thank you.

480
22:37.000 --> 22:38.330
-Thank you. -Thank you.

481
23:00.200 --> 23:01.200
Involuntary neurological reflexes

482
23:01.200 --> 23:01.790
have nothing to do with

483
23:01.790 --> 23:02.960
the probability of regaining consciousness.

484
23:02.960 --> 23:04.640
You're giving Zhang Jiao's parents hope now.

485
23:04.640 --> 23:05.830
If Jiao really doesn't wake up,

486
23:05.830 --> 23:07.680
they will be even more desperate.

487
23:07.680 --> 23:09.270
They just

488
23:09.750 --> 23:10.400
went through

489
23:10.400 --> 23:12.200
that emotional roller coaster.

490
23:16.160 --> 23:16.830
Mingming,

491
23:17.400 --> 23:19.200
Zhengliang did the right thing.

492
23:19.350 --> 23:20.550
If he hadn't said something reassuring,

493
23:20.550 --> 23:23.150
that couple wouldn't have been able to hold on.

494
23:23.610 --> 23:26.740
[Friendly Reminder]

495
23:31.480 --> 23:32.830
So he can tell

496
23:32.830 --> 23:34.360
comforting lies after all.

497
23:57.830 --> 23:59.790
Dad, you had a night shift too?

498
23:59.960 --> 24:01.110
I just got back.

499
24:10.920 --> 24:11.920
Son, you're back.

500
24:12.000 --> 24:12.790
I'm back.

501
24:12.790 --> 24:13.830
You and your dad should get some sleep.

502
24:13.830 --> 24:15.000
I'm off to work.

503
24:17.510 --> 24:18.310
Well,

504
24:18.440 --> 24:20.200
let me get you 2 boxes of milk.

505
24:20.880 --> 24:21.510
No need.

506
24:21.510 --> 24:22.400
You already have one.

507
24:22.400 --> 24:23.240
Is one box enough?

508
24:23.240 --> 24:23.830
Yeah.

509
24:35.920 --> 24:36.830
I'm telling you,

510
24:36.830 --> 24:38.030
wonders never cease.

511
24:38.030 --> 24:38.590
What's wrong?

512
24:38.590 --> 24:40.350
Our son has suddenly started reading books.

513
24:40.350 --> 24:42.030
He's finally trying to improve himself.

514
24:42.030 --> 24:43.440
Seriously, it's been so many years.

515
24:43.440 --> 24:44.440
I've never seen

516
24:44.440 --> 24:45.160
him read at home.

517
24:45.160 --> 24:46.680
He only started reading now?

518
24:46.680 --> 24:48.030
It's already too late.

519
24:50.440 --> 24:52.310
Well, aren't you starting to read too?

520
24:52.310 --> 24:53.400
How old are you?

521
24:53.400 --> 24:54.400
And it's not too late for you?

522
24:54.400 --> 24:55.930
Because I'm getting older,

523
24:55.960 --> 24:57.640
I have to hurry up and read now.

524
24:57.640 --> 24:59.110
Look at Liu Zhengliang. He's so young,

525
24:59.110 --> 25:01.370
and his skills are about to surpass mine.

526
25:06.830 --> 25:08.400
I really can't get into it.

527
25:16.510 --> 25:22.760
[Mingming] [Are you home?]

528
25:31.310 --> 25:32.300
[Are you asleep?]

529
25:32.320 --> 25:34.600
[Mingming]

530
25:34.650 --> 25:38.100
[Are you studying?]

531
25:43.190 --> 25:54.880
[Are you studying?]

532
25:54.970 --> 26:02.030
[Chen Junnan]

533
26:02.070 --> 26:08.760
[Sleeping. Do not disturb.]

534
26:25.270 --> 26:28.550
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

535
26:28.440 --> 26:30.000
Squeeze hard. Squeeze.

536
26:31.240 --> 26:31.750
Right.

537
26:32.270 --> 26:33.070
Okay.

538
26:33.790 --> 26:35.350
Come on, lift this leg.

539
26:35.350 --> 26:36.000
Xiaomei.

540
26:35.380 --> 26:38.750
[Nurses' Station]

541
26:36.000 --> 26:38.400
Give me the last patient's medical record.

542
26:42.000 --> 26:43.060
This one, this one.

543
26:47.640 --> 26:48.590
Okay, this one.

544
26:48.880 --> 26:50.750
Come on, this leg, lift.

545
26:52.070 --> 26:52.880
Okay.

546
26:52.880 --> 26:53.720
Cui Jia.

547
26:53.720 --> 26:54.880
This is Cui Jia.

548
26:55.200 --> 26:57.790
She was hit on the head with a club,

549
26:58.240 --> 27:00.550
resulting in an open traumatic brain injury.

550
27:00.550 --> 27:01.350
Take a look.

551
27:01.590 --> 27:03.520
Her recovery has been pretty good.

552
27:03.590 --> 27:04.270
Dr. Liu

553
27:04.270 --> 27:05.790
removed the hematoma very thoroughly

554
27:05.790 --> 27:07.680
and preserved her brain tissue quite well.

555
27:07.680 --> 27:08.350
So far,

556
27:08.350 --> 27:10.720
she hasn't shown any signs of lasting complications.

557
27:10.720 --> 27:11.510
Doctor.

558
27:13.000 --> 27:13.830
Will I need

559
27:13.830 --> 27:15.310
reconstructive surgery?

560
27:16.790 --> 27:18.320
We'd do it in about 3 months.

561
27:18.680 --> 27:19.880
We'd use a titanium mesh

562
27:19.880 --> 27:21.070
or PEEK material

563
27:21.110 --> 27:22.480
to repair your skull.

564
27:22.550 --> 27:23.960
I don't want the surgery.

565
27:25.790 --> 27:28.050
When's the earliest I can be discharged?

566
27:31.160 --> 27:32.110
At the earliest,

567
27:32.240 --> 27:33.830
you can be discharged next week.

568
27:33.830 --> 27:34.920
The skull reconstruction surgery

569
27:34.920 --> 27:36.120
is entirely up to you.

570
27:36.240 --> 27:37.030
My child,

571
27:37.110 --> 27:38.310
the doctor said

572
27:38.310 --> 27:39.200
if you don't get the surgery,

573
27:39.200 --> 27:41.000
you'll have 2 dents on your head.

574
27:41.350 --> 27:42.160
From a distance,

575
27:42.160 --> 27:43.550
you'll look like a gourd.

576
27:43.550 --> 27:45.210
When you walk down the street,

577
27:45.400 --> 27:46.270
won't people

578
27:46.270 --> 27:47.550
think you're an alien?

579
27:47.550 --> 27:48.200
Mom.

580
27:51.310 --> 27:53.310
You think I want to skip the surgery?

581
27:55.070 --> 27:57.270
We simply can't afford it.

582
27:59.310 --> 28:00.440
It's all my fault.

583
28:02.750 --> 28:03.830
I don't want you

584
28:03.830 --> 28:05.890
to go further into debt because of me.

585
28:11.110 --> 28:13.750
The Neurosurgical Department has been doing well this month.

586
28:13.750 --> 28:15.270
But there's still room for improvement.

587
28:15.270 --> 28:15.750
Okay.

588
28:16.790 --> 28:19.120
Take the patient we just saw, for example.

589
28:19.720 --> 28:21.510
We must make sure she gets her skull reconstruction done

590
28:21.510 --> 28:22.750
at our hospital.

591
28:23.590 --> 28:24.880
She needs the surgery.

592
28:26.110 --> 28:27.720
She just hasn't thought it through yet.

593
28:27.720 --> 28:28.550
If she figures it out later

594
28:28.550 --> 28:30.210
and goes to another hospital,

595
28:30.640 --> 28:31.920
it'll be our loss.

596
28:31.920 --> 28:32.400
Yes.

597
28:37.720 --> 28:38.920
Goodbye, President.

598
28:41.380 --> 28:44.960
[Quiet]

599
28:41.960 --> 28:43.270
I'll leave this to you.

600
28:43.790 --> 28:45.190
Make sure you get it done.

601
28:45.510 --> 28:46.750
Didn't I just say

602
28:46.790 --> 28:47.720
it's her choice?

603
28:48.000 --> 28:49.330
She will choose to do it.

604
28:49.750 --> 28:51.350
We'll make sure it gets done.

605
28:51.720 --> 28:52.320
Good luck.

606
28:52.830 --> 28:54.550
I'll go withdraw all 6,000 yuan

607
28:54.550 --> 28:55.510
from the card.

608
28:55.590 --> 28:57.850
You go borrow some more from her Aunt Sun.

609
29:03.680 --> 29:04.830
The president is right.

610
29:04.830 --> 29:06.560
She needs the reconstruction.

611
29:06.880 --> 29:08.750
She'll have to get the surgery sooner or later.

612
29:08.750 --> 29:10.590
Most of the cost is for the medical materials.

613
29:10.590 --> 29:11.750
The hospital doesn't make much profit from it.

614
29:11.750 --> 29:13.590
So we're not making money at the patient's expense.

615
29:13.590 --> 29:15.000
Besides, it'll be cheaper for her

616
29:15.000 --> 29:16.720
to have it done here than at other hospitals.

617
29:16.720 --> 29:17.510
I don't care.

618
29:17.720 --> 29:18.960
You made the promise,

619
29:18.960 --> 29:20.220
so you go persuade her.

620
29:22.590 --> 29:24.070
The key is to find out

621
29:24.070 --> 29:24.960
if her family can actually

622
29:24.960 --> 29:25.960
afford it.

623
29:26.400 --> 29:27.070
What if

624
29:27.070 --> 29:28.920
they're truly at the end of their rope?

625
29:28.920 --> 29:31.640
No matter how hard we try to persuade them, it won't work.

626
29:31.640 --> 29:33.370
Medical care is not a business.

627
29:34.680 --> 29:35.640
But doctors

628
29:35.640 --> 29:37.240
have to make a living, right?

629
29:38.200 --> 29:38.720
Excuse me,

630
29:38.720 --> 29:39.790
which way

631
29:39.790 --> 29:40.790
to Cui Jia's ward?

632
29:44.380 --> 29:47.290
[Divorce Agreement]

633
29:45.110 --> 29:46.910
I've signed the divorce papers.

634
29:48.550 --> 29:49.950
You should sign them too.

635
29:51.070 --> 29:52.800
There's no point in carrying on

636
29:53.480 --> 29:54.510
like this.

637
29:57.480 --> 29:59.350
I've squandered all your money.

638
30:00.400 --> 30:02.600
I don't want any compensation from you.

639
30:03.240 --> 30:04.510
I told the judge

640
30:05.750 --> 30:06.810
that I forgave you.

641
30:08.830 --> 30:11.230
But let's not hold each other back anymore.

642
30:14.480 --> 30:15.200
You need

643
30:15.200 --> 30:17.660
a good woman who knows how to run a household.

644
30:18.270 --> 30:19.200
I'm not.

645
30:20.720 --> 30:22.720
I'm going to the South to try my luck,

646
30:23.550 --> 30:24.880
to see

647
30:26.270 --> 30:27.800
where my limits really lie.

648
30:30.440 --> 30:32.500
He's not going to hit her again, is he?

649
30:33.070 --> 30:34.640
Don't goad him anymore.

650
30:34.640 --> 30:35.770
Just watch quietly.

651
30:37.550 --> 30:38.640
I was wrong.

652
30:38.830 --> 30:40.230
I shouldn't have hit you.

653
30:40.720 --> 30:41.480
If you want a divorce, fine.

654
30:41.480 --> 30:43.210
I'll even accept going to jail.

655
30:43.440 --> 30:44.840
Can you just settle down?

656
30:46.750 --> 30:47.960
I won't spend my whole life

657
30:47.960 --> 30:49.310
holed up in this dump.

658
30:50.960 --> 30:52.440
I'm so beautiful.

659
30:53.790 --> 30:55.920
Is this really all life has to offer me?

660
30:58.510 --> 31:00.070
I don't accept it.

661
31:05.970 --> 31:09.320
[Pizza Hut]

662
31:13.160 --> 31:14.830
Try this. Double cheese.

663
31:14.830 --> 31:15.440
Thank you.

664
31:15.750 --> 31:17.070
You ordered too much. We can't finish this.

665
31:17.070 --> 31:18.930
Let's have a taste of everything.

666
31:21.110 --> 31:22.550
Speaking of Cui Jia,

667
31:23.400 --> 31:24.750
at 16 or 17,

668
31:24.750 --> 31:27.110
she was already hanging around with a gangster.

669
31:27.110 --> 31:28.200
That gangster

670
31:28.830 --> 31:29.880
was young and hot-blooded,

671
31:29.880 --> 31:30.790
always getting into fights.

672
31:30.790 --> 31:32.520
She fell for him at first sight.

673
31:35.350 --> 31:36.680
Don't go! Don't go!

674
31:36.680 --> 31:37.350
Just you wait. This is not over.

675
31:36.740 --> 31:38.290
[Xingyi Hotel]

676
31:37.350 --> 31:38.030
Wait here, you!

677
31:38.030 --> 31:38.590
Wait here!

678
31:38.290 --> 31:43.690
[Jiuyue Hotel]

679
31:43.830 --> 31:44.890
So, what do you say?

680
31:48.270 --> 31:49.550
I'll take you as my man.

681
31:51.350 --> 31:52.030
Let's get married.

682
31:52.030 --> 31:54.720
Cui Jia's ambitions were sky-high.

683
31:54.920 --> 31:55.960
She was always

684
31:55.960 --> 31:57.270
chasing one dubious investment

685
31:57.270 --> 31:58.400
after another:

686
31:59.070 --> 32:00.790
massive afforestation projects,

687
32:00.790 --> 32:02.350
crowdfunded tree planting,

688
32:02.350 --> 32:04.440
ant farming,

689
32:04.720 --> 32:05.960
and...

690
32:06.830 --> 32:08.160
speculating in silver,

691
32:08.310 --> 32:09.960
bogus stock-trading platforms,

692
32:09.960 --> 32:12.020
and even so-called national assets.

693
32:12.550 --> 32:13.750
Back then, that gangster

694
32:13.750 --> 32:14.550
had made a little money

695
32:14.550 --> 32:15.550
running a small business.

696
32:15.550 --> 32:19.270
But no amount of money could withstand that kind of reckless spending.

697
32:19.270 --> 32:20.720
Plant trees.

698
32:20.720 --> 32:21.790
And it's eco-friendly.

699
32:21.790 --> 32:23.480
Then our 20,000...

700
32:22.940 --> 32:24.610
[Plant Trees, Grow Rich]

701
32:24.240 --> 32:25.240
26,600 yuan.

702
32:25.350 --> 32:26.280
I got here first!

703
32:26.310 --> 32:27.240
I got here first!

704
32:28.830 --> 32:30.550
I got here first! I got here first!

705
32:30.550 --> 32:31.640
I want 20 mu!

706
32:32.150 --> 32:33.200
Twenty mu?

707
32:33.750 --> 32:34.830
How much?

708
32:34.960 --> 32:36.270
53,200 yuan!

709
32:36.310 --> 32:37.240
Deal!

710
32:37.240 --> 32:38.790
Is this Yilitong Company?

711
32:39.640 --> 32:41.160
This is Cui Jia!

712
32:41.160 --> 32:43.400
I bought ants from you.

713
32:45.160 --> 32:46.020
Let me tell you,

714
32:46.830 --> 32:48.350
I've raised them

715
32:48.350 --> 32:49.790
really well.

716
32:49.880 --> 32:51.350
They've grown so big.

717
32:51.830 --> 32:53.310
When are you coming to collect them?

718
32:53.310 --> 32:55.110
It wasn't just his money she lost.

719
32:55.110 --> 32:56.160
She blew through

720
32:56.160 --> 32:57.590
both her parents' and her in-laws'

721
32:57.590 --> 32:58.920
retirement funds and savings too.

722
32:58.920 --> 33:00.180
Just give it all to her.

723
33:15.200 --> 33:17.200
All the money's been swindled away.

724
33:17.590 --> 33:18.720
Let's get a divorce.

725
33:19.070 --> 33:21.200
How will you survive if you divorce me?

726
33:22.110 --> 33:23.030
Just make sure

727
33:24.480 --> 33:26.140
you're doing okay on your own.

728
33:26.270 --> 33:27.270
I asked Cui Jia,

729
33:28.480 --> 33:30.790
"Where do you want to go in the South?

730
33:32.150 --> 33:33.410
Do you have any plans?"

731
33:34.680 --> 33:37.480
She said, "Once you cross Shanhai Pass,

732
33:37.830 --> 33:39.360
you're in the South, right?

733
33:40.400 --> 33:41.720
I don't have any plans."

734
33:41.720 --> 33:42.790
When I heard that,

735
33:42.920 --> 33:46.050
I thought that blow didn't even knock any sense into her.

736
33:46.400 --> 33:47.920
She really is infuriating.

737
33:47.920 --> 33:50.720
But still, no matter what, he shouldn't have hit her.

738
33:50.720 --> 33:51.440
Yes.

739
33:51.640 --> 33:52.750
Hitting someone is never acceptable.

740
33:52.750 --> 33:53.420
But every situation

741
33:53.420 --> 33:54.510
has to have an outcome.

742
33:54.510 --> 33:55.920
And now there is one.

743
33:56.640 --> 33:57.700
They're divorced,

744
33:57.880 --> 33:59.070
and that gangster is in jail.

745
33:59.070 --> 34:00.440
And your task

746
34:00.680 --> 34:02.210
can't be completed either.

747
34:03.830 --> 34:05.110
Well... Anyway...

748
34:07.270 --> 34:09.270
her family really has no money left.

749
34:10.630 --> 34:11.960
From what you said,

750
34:12.710 --> 34:13.920
I think she'll have a hard time

751
34:13.920 --> 34:15.030
down south too.

752
34:16.320 --> 34:17.480
What's the big deal?

753
34:17.590 --> 34:19.230
These days, nobody starves.

754
34:19.630 --> 34:21.000
If she can't make it,

755
34:21.110 --> 34:22.370
she can just come back.

756
34:22.440 --> 34:24.030
The problem is, once she's seen

757
34:24.030 --> 34:26.280
the dazzling splendor of a big city,

758
34:26.280 --> 34:28.510
along with all the struggles beneath the surface,

759
34:28.510 --> 34:30.070
her horizons will have broadened.

760
34:30.070 --> 34:32.270
But if she still can't find her footing,

761
34:33.670 --> 34:34.870
the harder she works,

762
34:35.630 --> 34:36.710
the more hopeless she might feel.

763
34:36.710 --> 34:38.150
Once her dreams are shattered

764
34:38.150 --> 34:40.679
and she finally accepts her fate, coming back

765
34:40.880 --> 34:44.480
might feel even worse than if she'd never left in the first place.

766
34:44.710 --> 34:46.670
Come on, guys, lift it!

767
34:50.610 --> 34:55.540
[1314; Funeral Wreath & Burial Clothes; Xiaoximen Branch]

768
35:04.630 --> 35:05.280
Awesome!

769
35:05.280 --> 35:05.920
Nice!

770
35:06.070 --> 35:06.550
Nice!

771
35:06.760 --> 35:08.690
These firecrackers were amazing.

772
35:08.760 --> 35:09.490
What a blast.

773
35:10.030 --> 35:10.630
Sis.

774
35:10.880 --> 35:11.340
That...

775
35:11.480 --> 35:14.030
What does that "branches of red flowers peeking over the wall" mean?

776
35:14.030 --> 35:16.070
Where does it look red?

777
35:17.590 --> 35:18.480
Isn't that it?

778
35:19.000 --> 35:21.550
In the corner, there are a few plum blossoms.

779
35:21.880 --> 35:23.590
They're the only ones blooming.

780
35:23.590 --> 35:25.110
And you can tell from far away

781
35:25.110 --> 35:26.070
that they're not snowflakes.

782
35:26.070 --> 35:26.710
Why?

783
35:27.550 --> 35:29.630
Because a hidden fragrance comes drifting.

784
35:29.630 --> 35:30.360
What?

785
35:30.360 --> 35:31.510
Do you even know which poem that's from?

786
35:31.510 --> 35:32.320
I don't know.

787
35:33.000 --> 35:34.670
Sis, what does our funeral business

788
35:34.670 --> 35:36.330
have to do with plum blossoms?

789
35:39.840 --> 35:41.110
Are you staging a coup?

790
35:42.400 --> 35:44.330
I decide what goes on my signboard.

791
35:45.070 --> 35:46.000
Liu Zhengguang.

792
35:47.710 --> 35:49.110
Where did you pop up from?

793
35:49.110 --> 35:50.040
What do you want?

794
35:50.630 --> 35:52.360
Come here. I need to talk to you.

795
35:53.920 --> 35:55.920
What's there to talk about with you?

796
35:57.280 --> 35:58.080
Let me ask you.

797
35:58.440 --> 36:00.400
Are you sure you're going to Beijing?

798
36:00.400 --> 36:01.190
I'm sure.

799
36:01.280 --> 36:02.150
I've already bought the ticket.

800
36:02.150 --> 36:03.480
I'm leaving on the 31st.

801
36:03.590 --> 36:04.880
Why not think it over once more,

802
36:04.880 --> 36:06.230
and be sure before you go?

803
36:06.230 --> 36:07.030
What's with you?

804
36:07.030 --> 36:08.710
You change your mind every single day.

805
36:08.710 --> 36:09.150
That's not

806
36:09.150 --> 36:11.080
what you were saying a few days ago.

807
36:13.070 --> 36:14.230
I have a classmate.

808
36:14.440 --> 36:16.320
His younger brother got his PhD this year.

809
36:16.320 --> 36:17.110
He sent out a bunch of resumes,

810
36:17.110 --> 36:18.800
but in the end, he still went back to his hometown.

811
36:18.800 --> 36:20.360
Do you think you're better than him?

812
36:20.360 --> 36:21.630
What's that supposed to mean?

813
36:21.630 --> 36:23.070
Are you saying my education isn't good enough

814
36:23.070 --> 36:25.070
and I won't make it in a big city, huh?

815
36:25.320 --> 36:26.360
Trying to scare me?

816
36:26.360 --> 36:27.320
Let me tell you,

817
36:27.510 --> 36:28.510
I've met plenty of people

818
36:28.510 --> 36:29.480
more outstanding than you,

819
36:29.480 --> 36:31.610
and in the end, they all went back home.

820
36:32.190 --> 36:33.960
And let me tell you something, Liu Zhengliang.

821
36:33.960 --> 36:35.710
I've been selling urns since I was a kid.

822
36:35.710 --> 36:36.400
I've seen more people off

823
36:36.400 --> 36:38.070
to their final resting places than you've ever met in your life.

824
36:38.070 --> 36:39.070
Just because you couldn't make it in a big city,

825
36:39.070 --> 36:41.470
do you think everyone is as clueless as you?

826
36:42.920 --> 36:44.360
With your anti-intellectual attitude,

827
36:44.360 --> 36:45.630
you'll never fit in a big city.

828
36:45.630 --> 36:47.490
Why even bother going to Beijing?

829
36:49.190 --> 36:50.840
Now you're attacking my IQ,

830
36:50.840 --> 36:51.320
huh?

831
36:51.400 --> 36:52.860
Saying I have a low IQ, huh?

832
36:53.110 --> 36:54.110
You have a high IQ.

833
36:54.230 --> 36:55.110
You're awesome.

834
36:55.110 --> 36:56.510
Y-You're a real powerhouse.

835
36:56.510 --> 36:57.070
You're highly educated.

836
36:57.070 --> 36:59.070
You're good at everything, and you know everything.

837
36:59.070 --> 37:00.230
But didn't you get

838
37:00.230 --> 37:00.840
sent packing back here

839
37:00.840 --> 37:01.900
from the South too?

840
37:02.110 --> 37:03.880
A-And now you're lecturing me?

841
37:04.150 --> 37:04.920
So I'm the only one

842
37:04.920 --> 37:06.000
you get to look down on, huh?

843
37:06.000 --> 37:07.460
Are you proud of yourself?

844
37:09.880 --> 37:10.810
You're nothing.

845
37:14.230 --> 37:15.440
Fine, fine.

846
37:17.440 --> 37:18.550
Do whatever you want.

847
37:18.550 --> 37:19.760
Nobody's stopping you.

848
37:19.760 --> 37:20.510
Psycho.

849
37:26.670 --> 37:27.600
Liu Zhengliang!

850
37:29.550 --> 37:30.320
Seriously,

851
37:30.320 --> 37:31.650
why are you so stubborn?

852
37:32.230 --> 37:33.490
Just say what you want.

853
37:34.280 --> 37:36.140
Don't you care about Zhengguang?

854
37:36.320 --> 37:38.120
Why can't you just say it nicely?

855
37:38.550 --> 37:39.630
Just tell him,

856
37:39.630 --> 37:41.630
"I care about you.

857
37:42.280 --> 37:43.030
I'm worried you

858
37:43.030 --> 37:43.840
won't be able to

859
37:43.840 --> 37:45.400
look after yourself out there." Right?

860
37:45.400 --> 37:46.110
You two are brothers.

861
37:46.110 --> 37:47.000
What can't you say to each other?

862
37:47.000 --> 37:47.760
Just talk to him nicely.

863
37:47.760 --> 37:49.320
What's it got to do with you?

864
37:49.630 --> 37:51.430
Who are you to tell me how to talk?

865
37:53.000 --> 37:54.330
Ungrateful again, huh?

866
37:56.190 --> 37:58.050
Then why won't you leave me alone?

867
37:58.070 --> 37:59.930
Are you a masochist or something?

868
38:03.360 --> 38:05.020
You're asking to get slapped!

869
38:06.320 --> 38:08.150
Who do you think you're talking to?

870
38:08.150 --> 38:09.550
I don't owe you anything.

871
38:10.440 --> 38:11.770
Freaking piece of work.

872
38:13.670 --> 38:14.480
From now on,

873
38:14.590 --> 38:16.590
I'd have to be crazy to be nice to you!

874
38:17.670 --> 38:19.360
Look at you, so full of yourself.

875
38:19.360 --> 38:20.190
Such a pain in the ass.

876
38:20.190 --> 38:21.190
Say one more word,

877
38:21.360 --> 38:22.690
and I'll knock you flat.

878
38:25.150 --> 38:26.110
Psycho.

879
38:27.320 --> 38:28.050
Thanks, man.

880
38:35.250 --> 38:38.400
[Nurses' Station]

881
38:39.800 --> 38:40.280
Miss,

882
38:40.280 --> 38:41.590
even if you're leaving like this,

883
38:41.590 --> 38:42.150
shouldn't you

884
38:42.150 --> 38:43.630
at least let your parents know

885
38:43.630 --> 38:44.590
and say goodbye?

886
38:45.590 --> 38:46.400
Yeah.

887
38:46.710 --> 38:47.920
You have to come back

888
38:48.630 --> 38:49.710
in 3 months

889
38:49.710 --> 38:51.030
for the skull reconstruction.

890
38:51.030 --> 38:52.800
Don't worry about the money.

891
38:53.440 --> 38:55.590
We'll do everything we can...

892
38:55.590 --> 38:57.790
to help you get some of the costs waived.

893
38:57.960 --> 38:59.400
I just look a bit ugly.

894
39:01.440 --> 39:03.900
I don't want to waste any more of their money.

895
39:04.590 --> 39:05.400
I can manage.

896
39:05.400 --> 39:06.110
No,

897
39:06.230 --> 39:07.880
it's not just about your appearance.

898
39:07.880 --> 39:09.230
If someone else gets hurt,

899
39:09.230 --> 39:10.710
they might just be sore for a while.

900
39:10.710 --> 39:12.000
But for you, it could be life-threatening.

901
39:12.000 --> 39:13.060
Do you understand?

902
39:18.150 --> 39:18.840
Right.

903
39:19.230 --> 39:20.070
Even if you decide not to

904
39:20.070 --> 39:21.190
have the skull reconstruction,

905
39:21.190 --> 39:22.190
at least get

906
39:22.190 --> 39:24.280
a protective cap for the missing parts of your skull.

907
39:24.280 --> 39:25.000
It would help

908
39:25.000 --> 39:26.060
protect your head.

909
39:36.960 --> 39:38.760
Do you guys think this will work?

910
39:41.590 --> 39:42.280
This...

911
39:48.150 --> 39:48.840
Thank you. Thank you.

912
39:48.840 --> 39:50.320
Are you sure you can manage like this?

913
39:50.320 --> 39:52.480
Even a sprain or fracture takes 100 days to heal.

914
39:52.480 --> 39:54.280
It's only been a little over 2 weeks for you.

915
39:54.280 --> 39:55.360
Running around everywhere

916
39:55.360 --> 39:56.360
is too dangerous.

917
39:57.030 --> 39:58.760
Isn't this a bit too makeshift?

918
40:05.760 --> 40:07.420
Everyone lives their own way.

919
40:08.670 --> 40:09.710
You can make do

920
40:10.590 --> 40:12.120
and still live a whole life.

921
40:14.150 --> 40:15.190
To this day,

922
40:15.190 --> 40:16.320
I still believe

923
40:16.440 --> 40:18.320
my best days are ahead of me.

924
40:19.070 --> 40:20.510
I'm going South to give it a shot.

925
40:20.510 --> 40:21.630
Once I make some real money,

926
40:21.630 --> 40:23.510
I'll come back and get my skull fixed.

927
40:23.510 --> 40:24.320
And then

928
40:24.320 --> 40:25.280
I promise I'll help you all

929
40:25.280 --> 40:26.080
hit your KPIs!

930
40:26.590 --> 40:27.960
This isn't about money.

931
40:28.400 --> 40:29.070
Yeah.

932
40:33.960 --> 40:34.590
Thanks.

933
40:38.400 --> 40:40.200
Be careful. You must be careful.

934
40:40.510 --> 40:41.550
Sir, take it slow.

935
40:44.800 --> 40:45.480
Take care!

936
40:47.260 --> 40:51.320
[Outpatient; Entrance]

937
40:47.400 --> 40:48.200
Let's go, sir.

938
40:51.760 --> 40:53.110
She's such a flake.

939
40:53.630 --> 40:55.190
She can barely take care of herself.

940
40:55.190 --> 40:57.190
How is she going to live from here on?

941
40:59.550 --> 41:01.150
A girl this funny

942
41:01.670 --> 41:03.130
won't have terrible luck.

943
41:04.280 --> 41:05.410
Let her try her luck.

944
41:06.230 --> 41:08.030
I'm even a little envious of her.

945
41:11.760 --> 41:13.890
I hope she makes something of herself.

946
41:16.590 --> 41:17.230
I still think

947
41:17.230 --> 41:19.090
she'd be better off staying here.

948
41:21.630 --> 41:22.560
Liu Zhengliang.

949
41:24.920 --> 41:28.350
[Outpatient; Entrance]

950
41:28.510 --> 41:29.840
Dr. Liu.

951
41:32.510 --> 41:33.280
Dr. Liu.

952
41:36.670 --> 41:38.760
Let's have a little chat today,

953
41:39.110 --> 41:39.970
heart to heart,

954
41:40.480 --> 41:41.920
straightforwardly and honestly,

955
41:41.920 --> 41:44.580
so we can both walk away with our dignity intact.

956
41:44.710 --> 41:46.960
But if you try to play games with me...

957
41:48.150 --> 41:48.760
Huh?

958
41:48.760 --> 41:50.440
You can go ask around about

959
41:51.760 --> 41:53.960
what I, Ai San, used to do.

960
41:57.670 --> 41:59.480
What's your deal...

961
42:01.190 --> 42:02.920
with our Ai Chen?

962
42:04.920 --> 42:06.150
Nothing.

963
42:09.510 --> 42:11.440
You're not being straight with me.

964
42:12.440 --> 42:13.550
We've all seen it.

965
42:14.630 --> 42:15.510
You...

966
42:16.190 --> 42:18.650
You've been hitting on our Ai Chen every day.

967
42:19.000 --> 42:19.760
You're a grown man;

968
42:19.760 --> 42:20.920
just admit it.

969
42:21.510 --> 42:23.070
I wasn't hitting on her.

970
42:23.230 --> 42:24.400
I don't like her.

971
42:24.400 --> 42:26.060
What am I supposed to admit to?

972
42:40.760 --> 42:41.880
Our Ai Chen

973
42:42.440 --> 42:44.320
has already started to like you.

974
42:45.400 --> 42:47.000
Who do you think you are

975
42:47.000 --> 42:48.400
to say you don't like her?

976
42:49.230 --> 42:49.960
Is our girl

977
42:49.960 --> 42:51.360
not good enough for you?

978
42:54.800 --> 42:55.590
Who is that?

979
42:56.630 --> 42:57.510
That's San.

980
43:00.070 --> 43:01.070
Which San?

981
43:03.510 --> 43:04.910
Ai Chen's father, Ai San.

982
43:05.280 --> 43:06.840
A big-time underworld figure back in the day.

983
43:06.840 --> 43:07.670
Very tough.

984
43:11.550 --> 43:12.590
Zhengliang offended him?
